From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] rockchip: boot_mode: an option for a board without a
 download key

Copyright (C) 2026 Olympian LED, Inc.

With a boot mode register (ROCKCHIP_BOOT_MODE_REG), U-Boot proper's
board_late_init() checks the download key and, when it reads as held,
writes BOOT_BROM_DOWNLOAD (0xEF08A53C) to that register and resets into
the BootROM's download mode, which waits for a USB host for ever. A
board with no download key has no use for that path, but it is linked
all the same, because rockchip_dnl_key_pressed() is weak.

ROCKCHIP_DOWNLOAD_KEY (default y, so nothing changes for any other
board) turns the check off: setup_boot_mode() no longer calls
rockchip_dnl_mode_check(), so neither it nor
set_back_to_bootrom_dnl_flag() is linked into U-Boot proper. TPL and
SPL still honor BOOT_BROM_DOWNLOAD when something else wrote it
(save_boot_params()).

The Rigol DHO800/DHO900 and MHO900 board needs the boot mode register
for that TPL check, and has no download key: SARADC channel 1 is not
wired, so mainline's ADC reading could only ever be wrong.

Signed-off-by: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-rockchip/Kconfig     | 12 ++++++++++++
 arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c |  3 ++-
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/Kconfig b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/Kconfig
index b99e3bcb..79379593 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/Kconfig
@@ -658,6 +658,18 @@ config ROCKCHIP_BOOT_MODE_REG
 	  The Soc will enter to different boot mode(defined in asm/arch-rockchip/boot_mode.h)
 	  according to the value from this register.
 
+config ROCKCHIP_DOWNLOAD_KEY
+	bool "Reset into the BootROM's download mode when the download key is held"
+	default y
+	help
+	  With a boot mode register, U-Boot proper reads the download key in
+	  board_late_init() (SARADC channel 1, or the board's own
+	  rockchip_dnl_key_pressed()) and, when it is held, writes
+	  BOOT_BROM_DOWNLOAD to the boot mode register and resets into the
+	  BootROM's download mode. Say n on a board that has no such key: U-Boot
+	  proper then never writes that value, while TPL and SPL still honor it
+	  when something else has written it (save_boot_params()).
+
 config ROCKCHIP_RK8XX_DISABLE_BOOT_ON_POWERON
 	bool "Disable device boot on power plug-in"
 	depends on PMIC_RK8XX
diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
index 55e94566..366cffa6 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
@@ -88,7 +88,8 @@ int setup_boot_mode(void)
 	void *reg = (void *)CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_BOOT_MODE_REG;
 	int boot_mode = readl(reg);
 
-	rockchip_dnl_mode_check();
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_DOWNLOAD_KEY))
+		rockchip_dnl_mode_check();
 
 	boot_mode = readl(reg);
 	debug("%s: boot mode 0x%08x\n", __func__, boot_mode);
